From 7613cb0cbe7e6549ecaba7e8cc811923c0fbad6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron Guise <aaron@guise.net.nz>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 14:17:13 +1200
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] build(docker): add multi-arch image publishing via
 Justfile :whale:

Adds build-multiarch/docker-publish recipes that cross-compile amd64+arm64
binaries natively with build.sh and assemble them into Dockerfile.fast
images, pushed as a combined manifest to docker.io/cybercinch/stalwart
tagged :latest and :<stalwart-version>. Credentials load from a local
.env (see .env.example). Also fixes Dockerfile.fast, which referenced a
non-existent resources/docker/entrypoint.sh and would not have built -
it now mirrors the official Dockerfile's runtime stage (non-root user,
healthcheck, volumes) but skips the in-container Rust build.
